  "worked_solution": "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13947117/assets/d00bb449e3525bed0543e690ef41895da5ad9bd28632f127aa7d8e5876ce7deb.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the second quadrant of the complex plane. Hence $\\frac{\\pi }{2}<\\operatorname{arg}\u2061(z)<\\pi .$ \n\nIf $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the negative real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}\u2061\\alpha  & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\alpha  & =\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}\u2061(z)=\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3}=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\n$$",
